# init.recovery.logd.rc
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS (do not delete)
# -----------------------------------
# TWRP-11's system/etc/init/hw/init.rc contains:
#     import /init.recovery.logd.rc
# and AOSP init's parser treats a failed `import` of a *file* as a FATAL parse
# error -> init aborts -> kernel panic ("Attempted to kill init!") -> the
# bootloader watchdog resets after ~8 s -> infinite boot loop / fastboot.
# (The init binary carries the string "Could not import directory '%s'" and
#  Parser::ParseConfig() calls init.abort() when an import cannot be read.)
#
# On the minimal TWRP manifest (platform_manifest_twrp_aosp / twrp-11) used by
# .github/workflows/build-twrp.yml, TWRP never ships this file, so the import
# dangles and recovery can never start. We satisfy it here.
#
# The full AOSP version of this file starts a `logd` service. That binary is
# deliberately NOT in this recovery ramdisk (TWRP does its own logging), so the
# body is intentionally empty: an empty .rc is valid and adds no behaviour.
# If you later add system/bin/logd to TW_RECOVERY_INCLUDE_PACKAGES, put the
# real service definition here.
